      "directNodeIds": [
        "math:real-exponent-laws",
        "cnm_h042"
      ],
      "explanation": "Since \\(8=2^3\\) and \\(32=2^5\\), rewriting with base \\(2\\) lets us compare the exponents. The power-of-a-power rule gives\n\\[\n8^x=32\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n(2^3)^x=2^5\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n2^{3x}=2^5.\n\\]\nBecause \\(2>1\\), its powers strictly increase as the real exponent increases. Thus equal powers of \\(2\\) must have equal exponents, so \\(3x=5\\). Dividing by \\(3\\) gives the unique solution \\(\\boxed{x=\\frac53}\\), choice B.",
      "id": "common-base-powers",
      "sourceRef": "amc/1962_AMC_12_Q04#common-base-powers",
      "title": "Rewrite with a common base"
    },
